{
  "requirement": "Each page has the same result fields as the originating tool. Text reads return\nsuccessive portions of text. Listings, outlines, and searches return successive\narrays of whole entries in their original order. Only a page with a successor\nincludes `next`.\n\nReusing a UUID returns the same page from the original snapshot, including the\nsame successor UUID if more remains. A malformed UUID, an unknown UUID, or a UUID\nfrom another conversation returns a tool error under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.tool_agent.isolation`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.pages.behavior`.\n\n**Same result fields as the originating tool.**\n- `search_pages_return_every_original_match_in_order` asserts each search page's `complete`, `search_id` and `matches` entries (`node`, `file`, `selector`, `excerpt`, `tag`).\n- `outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items` asserts that outline pages keep `node`, and that items keep `file`, `selector` and `kind`.\n- `listing_continuations_return_complete_paths_from_the_original_listing` asserts each listing entry's `node` and `data`.\n- `source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read` asserts `node` and `text` on read_source pages. `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` asserts `text` on graph read pages.\n\n**Text reads return successive portions.**\n- The graph read test concatenates the pages and compares the result to the original, which contains multi-byte characters.\n- The source read test joins the pages and compares them to the original.\n- The outline root-read loop in `outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items` concatenates `text` and compares it to the original.\n\n**Listings, outlines and searches return whole entries in original order.**\n- The search test compares every entry in order against the original snapshot after the file has been changed, and checks that the count equals the number of lines.\n- The outline test checks all 401 items in order.\n- The listing test checks the 2000 files in order, even after a file is added mid-pagination.\n- The `Pages` unit test covers the `text`, `files` and `items` fields.\n\n**Only a page with a successor includes `next`.**\n- The graph read test asserts `next` is present only on the first of two pages.\n- The loops in the search, outline and listing tests stop on an absent `next`, and the non-empty-page assertions in the search and outline tests rule out a trailing empty page.\n- The source tools test asserts that a single-page result has no `next`.\n\n**Replay returns the same page and the same successor UUID.**\n- `text_listing_and_outline_continuations_replay_the_same_page_and_successor` re-fetches the second and third pages by UUID and compares their text. That text includes `next`, so the successor UUID is compared too.\n- `search_obligations_follow_delivery_and_keep_the_original_snapshot` re-requests `next` after the source changed and asserts identical text.\n\n**Errors under isolation.**\n- A malformed UUID (`\"invalid\"`) and an unknown UUID (all zeros) both error in the outline test. The `Pages` unit test also checks that a fresh `Pages` rejects an unknown UUID.\n- A UUID from another conversation is rejected in two places. `graph_page_ids_from_a_populated_peer_conversation_are_rejected` checks that the foreign UUID returns an error result containing \"unknown page\". The search test checks that a peer session's `get_next_page` fails.\n\nI found no obligation without a test and no marking gap.",
  "references": "ae98823fd5a9631c9f842bdebff51d78a9833a9875e9f065ec47ed447303c383",
